==English==

===Alternative forms===
* [[addon]]

===Etymology===
[[add]] + [[on]]

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun}}

# Something which can be appended to something else.
# {{computing|hardware|software}} A [[software]] extension or [[hardware]] [[peripheral]] that provides additional functions or customization for a core application or system.
#* '''2010''', Kenneth Baldauf, Ralph Stair, ''Succeeding with Technology'' (page 77)
#*: Microdrives that can hold several gigabytes (see Figure 2.20) have been available as '''add-ons''' for portable devices.

====Synonyms====
* [[plug-in]], [[add-in]]

